    "kernel_code": "1: import torch\n2: import triton\n3: import triton.language as tl\n4: \n5: \n6: @triton.jit\n7: def rotary_kernel(\n8:     OUT, X, COS, SIN,\n9:     seqlen, nheads, rotary_dim_half,\n10:     stride_out_seqlen, stride_out_nheads, stride_out_headdim,\n11:     stride_x_seqlen, stride_x_nheads, stride_x_headdim,\n12:     INTERLEAVED: tl.constexpr,\n13:     BLOCK_H: tl.constexpr, BLOCK_M: tl.constexpr, BLOCK_K: tl.constexpr,\n14: ):\n15:     pid_head = tl.program_id(0)\n16:     pid_m = tl.program_id(1)\n17:     rh = pid_head * BLOCK_H + tl.arange(0, BLOCK_H)\n18:     rm = pid_m * BLOCK_M + tl.arange(0, BLOCK_M)\n19:     rk_half = tl.arange(0, BLOCK_K // 2)\n20: \n21:     COS = COS + (rm[:, None] * rotary_dim_half + rk_half[None, :])\n22:     SIN = SIN + (rm[:, None] * rotary_dim_half + rk_half[None, :])\n23:     mask_cs = (rm[:, None] < seqlen) & (rk_half[None, :] < rotary_dim_half)\n24:     cos = tl.load(COS, mask=mask_cs, other=1.0).to(tl.float32)\n25:     sin = tl.load(SIN, mask=mask_cs, other=0.0).to(tl.float32)\n26: \n27:     if not INTERLEAVED:\n28:         X_ptrs = X + (rh[:, None, None] * stride_x_nheads + rm[None, :, None] * stride_x_seqlen + rk_half[None, None, :] * stride_x_headdim)\n29:         OUT_ptrs = OUT + (rh[:, None, None] * stride_out_nheads + rm[None, :, None] * stride_out_seqlen + rk_half[None, None, :] * stride_out_headdim)\n30:         mask = (rh[:, None, None] < nheads) & (rm[None, :, None] < seqlen) & (rk_half[None, None, :] < rotary_dim_half)\n31:         x0 = tl.load(X_ptrs, mask=mask, other=0.0).to(tl.float32)\n32:         x1 = tl.load(X_ptrs + rotary_dim_half * stride_x_headdim, mask=mask, other=0.0).to(tl.float32)\n33:         o0 = x0 * cos - x1 * sin\n34:         o1 = x0 * sin + x1 * cos\n35:         tl.store(OUT_ptrs, o0, mask=mask)\n36:         tl.store(OUT_ptrs + rotary_dim_half * stride_out_headdim, o1, mask=mask)\n37:     else:\n38:         rk = tl.arange(0, BLOCK_K)\n39:         X_ptrs = X + (rh[:, None, None] * stride_x_nheads + rm[None, :, None] * stride_x_seqlen + rk[None, None, :] * stride_x_headdim)\n40:         OUT_ptrs = OUT + (rh[:, None, None] * stride_out_nheads + rm[None, :, None] * stride_out_seqlen + rk[None, None, :] * stride_out_headdim)\n41:         mask = (rh[:, None, None] < nheads) & (rm[None, :, None] < seqlen) & (rk[None, None, :] < 2 * rotary_dim_half)\n42:         x = tl.load(X_ptrs, mask=mask, other=0.0).to(tl.float32)\n43:         x0, x1 = tl.split(tl.reshape(x, [BLOCK_H, BLOCK_M, BLOCK_K // 2, 2]))\n44:         o0 = x0 * cos - x1 * sin\n45:         o1 = x0 * sin + x1 * cos\n46:         o = tl.reshape(tl.join(o0, o1), [BLOCK_H, BLOCK_M, BLOCK_K])\n47:         tl.store(OUT_ptrs, o, mask=mask)\n48: \n49: \n50: def apply_rotary(x: torch.Tensor, cos: torch.Tensor, sin: torch.Tensor, interleaved: bool) -> torch.Tensor:\n51:     \"\"\"x: (seqlen, nheads, headdim). cos/sin: (seqlen, headdim//2).\"\"\"\n52:     seqlen, nheads, headdim = x.shape\n53:     rotary_dim_half = headdim // 2\n54:     out = torch.empty_like(x)\n55:     BLOCK_K = triton.next_power_of_2(headdim)\n56:     grid = (nheads, seqlen)\n57:     rotary_kernel[grid](\n58:         out, x, cos, sin,\n59:         seqlen, nheads, rotary_dim_half,\n60:         out.stride(0), out.stride(1), out.stride(2),\n61:         x.stride(0), x.stride(1), x.stride(2),\n62:         INTERLEAVED=interleaved, BLOCK_H=1, BLOCK_M=1, BLOCK_K=BLOCK_K,\n63:     )\n64:     return out",
    "passed": "unknown",
    "problem_text": "Operation: rotary position embeddings (RoPE)\n(Dao-AILab/flash-attention, flash_attn/ops/triton/rotary.py::rotary_kernel).\n\n`apply_rotary(x, cos, sin, interleaved)` must rotate each pair of feature\ndimensions of x by the position-dependent angle encoded in cos/sin, so that\nthe dot product of a rotated query and a rotated key depends on their relative\nposition.\n\nTwo pairings are in use in the field and the kernel implements both behind the\n`interleaved` flag:\n  - interleaved=False: dimension i is paired with dimension i + headdim/2\n  - interleaved=True:  dimension 2i is paired with dimension 2i+1\n\nThe specification does not mandate which pairing a model uses; it requires\nonly that a given model apply the same one consistently to both q and k.\n",
